{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/91033-setting-hack-it-s-your-fault","id":91033,"title":"Setting hack: it's your fault","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-14T13:00:37-07:00","id":91033,"title":"Setting hack: it's your fault","content":"The creation myth of the Forsaken is a morality tale that carries a clear message: the Wolf must hunt. The Forsaken are to hunt down spirits, people, werewolves and anything else that might threaten the fragile balance between Shadow and Flesh - the other option is chaos; the two worlds destroying each other.<br /> <br /> In this setting hack, I'd like to mess with these assumptions a bit.<br /> <br /> Thesis: the Forsaken are wrong. In the absence of external influence, Shadow and Flesh reach a natural equilibrium. Loci dry up. Spirits and humans stay where they should; and the efforts of the spiders and rats mostly cancel each other out.<br /> <br /> It takes an external influence to hurt this balance. That's werewolves. Simply by being half flesh half spirit abominations, they disrupt the natural state of balance between worlds. In territories owned by wolves, loci happen naturally and the Shadow seeks to enter the Flesh.<br /> <br /> This is not a function of the duties of the Forsaken but their nature. They can't help it.<br /> <br /> This does not make the Pure right (or sane, or nice, or the good guys); simply by being werewolves, they too attract spiritual badness. They only make bad things worse by serving their spirit lords instead of hunting them like they should.<br /> <br /> Most werewolves wise about the ways of the Shadow - the most experienced Ithaeur and Bone Shadows - know this, and how they're to blame for the damage they cause. It's a hard thing to admit, though, as it calls to question many of the basic assumptions of their faith.<br /> <br /> Functionally, this setting hack doesn't do much to change the game - the Wolf must still hunt, even if he himself is the reason there's prey. It casts a little doubt on the mission of the Forsaken, though.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-14T13:57:58-07:00","id":91079,"title":"","content":"Oooh, I like this. It also kind of helps to negate the Spirit Cop aspect of the game that people tend to not like so much, since it's really just werewolves cleaning up the byproduct of being werewolves, ie trying to keep from being the cause of bad things.<br /> <br /> It also encourages spirit stuff to be more centered around werewolves -- if werewolves cause loci, then why wouldn't spirits try to gather around them. And more clever spirits would want to manipulate the wolves into keeping the good things coming by erasing any ties they might have to the world of Flesh. . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2230-murder-chan","name":"Murder-chan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-15T04:02:26-07:00","id":91533,"title":"","content":"Very, very good. It is a deceptively simple change with a lot of implications. I love it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}